The image includes a voice and software from other projects:

- The voice, Piper's en_GB-alba-medium
  (https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/tree/v1.0.0/en/en_GB/alba/medium),
  fetched at build time and checked against src/radio/voices/SHA256SUMS; this
  repository holds only its sums. Its model card is in
  licenses/en_GB-alba-medium.MODEL_CARD. The voice is trained on the Alba speech
  corpus by Cassia Valentini-Botinhao and Junichi Yamagishi, University of
  Edinburgh (2019), https://datashare.ed.ac.uk/handle/10283/3270, licensed under
  the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. The model was fine-tuned from
  Piper's U.S. English lessac voice by the Piper project. Those Who Run uses the
  voice unchanged.
- Piper (piper-tts, https://github.com/OHF-Voice/piper1-gpl), GPL-3.0: the
  speech synthesis.
- discord.py (https://github.com/Rapptz/discord.py), MIT, with PyNaCl
  (Apache-2.0) and davey (MIT): the Discord voice connection.
- FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org), LGPL-2.1-or-later and GPL-2.0-or-later as Debian
  builds it, and libopus (https://opus-codec.org), BSD-3-Clause, installed from
  Debian's packages: resampling and encoding the audio played in Discord.
